  "notes": "Two parallel failure chains modeled (86C and 86D) since these are two physically distinct solenoid valve failures on two independent MSIVs, both stemming from the same cause. Inboard MSIVs are mentioned as having performed satisfactorily (design redundancy) but this is not modeled as BACKED_UP_BY since it describes a different, independent valve fulfilling the same isolation function per design, not a stated-operable backup system during an inoperability window in the BACKED_UP_BY sense used for ECCS backups. Cause code B (Design/Manufacturing/Installation/Construction Deficiency) taken verbatim per FORM-366 block 13 cause code, though category label is a standard NRC cause-code mapping since FORM-366 fields left cause_code/category as TBD/provisional but block_13 explicitly lists cause 'B' for the component row, which governs per rule 4."
